Third-party notices
===================

This repository vendors nothing. libstarkbank.a and libstarkbank.dylib /
libstarkbank.so contain only the original work LICENSE covers, and link the
libraries below.

The bundle is different, and that is the whole reason this file matters:
`make bundle` produces libstarkbank_full.a and libstarkbank_full.dylib /
libstarkbank_full.so with core-c, ecdsa-c and libsecp256k1 statically inside,
so anyone who receives a bundle artifact receives those works too and these
notices travel with it. `make bundle-curl` adds core-c's optional libcurl
transport, which links libcurl dynamically.

